Notices
=======

What the programs and files this repository builds for the Echos contain of
others' work, and the notices their licences ask to go with them.

Every update bundle carries this file as NOTICE beside the programs, and so
does every install from the PC (scripts/bundle.sh, deploy.sh,
install-system.sh, install-boot.sh): with the opening, the part "Every model"
and the parts that name the model, and each "Full text:" line replaced by the
whole of that file of the repository (scripts/notice.py).

This project's own code is under the MIT licence (LICENSE in the repository).
Its source, and everything needed to build each model's programs from it
(make DEVICE=<codename> STUBS=1, with no files of Amazon's), is at
https://github.com/Gamer92000/echo-dot-assist, the release of the bundle's
version (VERSION beside this file) under the tag v<version>.

Nothing of Amazon's is in the bundles: firmware, libraries and wake word models
come from the Echo itself and stay Amazon's.


