The Echo 4 (laser)
==================

The Echo 4's bundles also carry the programs of its Thread and Zigbee radio:
gprcp (scripts/gprcp-build.sh), otbr-agent, otbr-agent-csl and ot-ctl
(scripts/otbr-build.sh), and this project's own rcpbridge and zigbeed. zigbeed
links Mbed TLS (above).

gprcp
-----

OpenThread's RCP on ot-qorvo's GP712 platform. src/gprcp/ is that platform:
its files keep their OpenThread headers (BSD-3-Clause, below); timed.c and
glibc_shim.c are this project's, and so are the edits to radio.c, system.c,
openthread-core-gp712-config.h and CMakeLists.txt.

It links Qorvo's libQorvoGP712_ftd.a statically (Qorvo/qpg-openthread,
commit 2762d55db1d218be57f251a8c8eafbb1938c36a7, gp712/lib), which is fetched
at build time and is not in this repository. It is licensed under Qorvo's
EULA (Qorvo_EULA.txt in that repository at that commit), which allows its use
only in combination with Qorvo silicon (the Echo 4's GP712 is) and requires
this notice:

    Copyright (c) 2017-2021, Qorvo Inc.

gprcp carries that line in itself too: `gprcp --notice` prints it on stderr.

gprcp also contains:

- OpenThread and ot-qorvo: BSD-3-Clause, under "OpenThread" below.
- Mbed TLS: Apache-2.0 (above).
- musl, the C library, and Zig's compiler_rt, linked statically by Zig: MIT,
  under "musl" and "Zig" below.

otbr-agent, otbr-agent-csl, ot-ctl
----------------------------------

ot-br-posix (https://github.com/openthread/ot-br-posix) with the options and
patches of scripts/otbr-build.sh. They contain:

- ot-br-posix and OpenThread: BSD-3-Clause, under "OpenThread" below.
- tcplp, OpenThread's TCP, much of it FreeBSD's: under "tcplp" below.
- Mbed TLS: Apache-2.0 (above).
- cJSON and cpp-httplib: MIT, under "cJSON" and "cpp-httplib" below.
- libc++ and libc++abi of the Android NDK r21e, linked statically: under
  "libc++" below.

